                            {
                                "example_id": "3cab45fc-f393-4f65-bd8c-a47d3df9f6b7",
                                "sense_id": "5f04c33a-7bd1-37a6-b98a-661fa7412829",
                                "text": "Thus, sitting where I was, I lit my candle once more, and then clambered across that great coffin which, for two hours or more, had been a mid-wall of partition between me and danger. But to get out of the niche was harder than to get in; for now that I had a candle to light me, I saw that the coffin, though sound enough to outer view, was wormed through and through, and little better than a rotten shell. So it was that I had some ado to get over it, not daring either to kneel upon it or to bring much weight to bear with my hand, lest it should go through."
                            }
